<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hunac Ceel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hunac Ceel is a figure of Maya tradition recorded in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/books-of-chilam-balam">Books of Chilam Balam</a> as the founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cocom">Cocom</a> rule at Mayapan in northern Yucatán. According to the chronicles he survived being thrown into the sacred cenote at Chichen Itza, proclaimed a prophecy and later brought down the lord of Chichen Itza. The accounts are partly legendary and their dating is uncertain.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hunac-ceel.jpg" alt="Hunac Ceel" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Salhedine · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cenote_Xtoloc_en_Chich%C3%A9n_Itz%C3%A1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
